-- title:
--   Integral closedness of the pole chart over a DVR
-- statement:
--   Let $N \ge 1$ and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \nmid N$. Write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8), the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of the rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$, and let $A =$ `chartAlgInf N ℓ` be the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra of the field `modularFunctionFieldFull N` consisting of the elements integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra generated by the single element $j^{-1}$ (the inverse of `jFull N`). Let $R'$ be a discrete valuation ring (a commutative domain) equipped with a $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-algebra structure and whose residue field has characteristic $\ell$, and let $K'$ be a field that is a fraction field of $R'$, also a $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-algebra compatibly with $R'$ (scalar tower). Assume that $K' \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} A$ is a domain and is integrally closed in its fraction field. Then $R' \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} A$ is a domain and is integrally closed.
--
--   This is the base-change step which propagates normality of the pole chart ($j^{-1}$-chart) of the Igusa model of the modular curve of level $N$ from the generic fibre to an arbitrary discrete valuation ring of residue characteristic $\ell \nmid N$, the good-reduction case. It is used in the construction of an injective algebra map out of a chart tensor with integrally closed target, [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_algHom_tensor_chartAlg_injective_isIntegrallyClosed`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.exists_algHom_tensor_chartAlg_injective_isIntegrallyClosed).
